 === Loosening the limitations of `InterceptionFactory`

 CDI 2.0 introduced the `InterceptionFactory` which can be used to intercept a bean created via producer methods.
 The specification is a bit vague when it comes to boundaries of this feature - can interfaces be used or are we limited to implementation classes only?
 While it is safe to assume only the later, Weld supports both.

 E.g. given `SomeImpl` is an implementation of interface `SomeInterface` and `InterceptThis` is an `InterceptorBinding`, both producers work:

 [source.JAVA, java]
 -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
     @Produces
     @ApplicationScoped
     public SomeImpl produceBeanBasedOnImplClass(InterceptionFactory<SomeImpl> interceptionFactory) {
         interceptionFactory.configure().add(InterceptThis.Literal.INSTANCE);
         return interceptionFactory.createInterceptedInstance(new SomeImpl());
     }

     @Produces
     @ApplicationScoped
     public SomeInterface produceBeanBasedOnInterface(InterceptionFactory<SomeInterface> interceptionFactory) {
         interceptionFactory.configure().add(InterceptThis.Literal.INSTANCE);
         return interceptionFactory.createInterceptedInstance(new SomeImpl());
     }
